{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-09-25T23:21:15.063Z","data":{"text":"Task 3 is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented mutation picking, running, and report reading for change 083, all within the task scope.\n\n**Production code:**\n- `src/core/run/verification.ts` — added an optional fifth `extraEnv` argument, applied after `OSQ_CHANGE`.\n- `src/core/trace/mutation-pick.ts` — `pickMutations` builds covered-function picks from a scenario index, function ranges, resolved scope, and the latest start/end measures data, with file-then-line ordering.\n- `src/core/run/mutation-report.ts` — untrusted report parsing with killed/survived/invalid counting, range filtering, and the 200-char replacement cut.\n- `src/core/run/mutation-run.ts` — one pick run with placeholder/env substitution, temp report folder, outcome classification, and cleanup.\n\n**Tests:**\n- `tests/mutation-pick.test.ts` — all \"Mutation picks\" scenarios plus non-opted-in capability, untested tagged function, and pick order.\n- `tests/mutation-run.test.ts` — fake command covering placeholders/env/`OSQ_CHANGE`, every status mapping, all invalid-report and command-failure paths, long replacements, and temp-folder removal.\n\nBoth the task `verify` (19 tests) and the proposal `verify` (`pnpm verify`: typecheck, build, full suite, lint) pass. Notable design note recorded in the result: core cannot import `harness/types`, so `mutation-report.ts` declares a structurally identical `MutationSurvivor`; the raw scope is passed to `pickMutations` since measures carry no explicit scope field."}}
